    "translation": "To all employees:\nThis is a notice from the Human Resources Department about the introduction of a flextime system. From April 1, to increase flexibility in how we work, a flextime system will be introduced company-wide. Working hours until now have been from 9:00 to 17:30, but from now on, as long as you are working during the core time of 10:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m., you may decide your own starting and finishing times. Daily working hours remain seven hours and thirty minutes, the same as before. Note that there will be no change to salaries accompanying this change.\nHowever, employees working in the factory and reception staff are excluded from this system due to the nature of their duties. For the excluded sections, a staggered-hours commuting system will be announced separately instead. Also, if an off-site meeting or training session falls within core time, leaving the office is permitted provided you obtain your supervisor's approval by the previous day.\nEmployees who wish to use the system should apply through the HR website by March 15. If no application is made by the deadline, you will remain on the current working hours for the time being; however, even after April, if you apply by the 10th of any month, you can begin using the system from the following month. For any questions, please contact Takahashi in the HR Department.",
