    "translation": "An announcement from the Human Resources Department about the introduction of a mentor program for new employees.\nIn recent years, the number of young employees leaving within three years of joining has been increasing, and one reason we often hear is that \"there is no one I can casually consult.\" Strengthening recruitment alone cannot solve this problem. Therefore, the company has decided to assign each new employee joining in April a mentor: a senior employee in their third to fifth year at the company.\nMentors will offer advice not only on how to carry out work, but also on workplace relationships and personal concerns. So that new employees can open up about things that are hard to tell their direct supervisor, mentors will always be chosen from a different department. Meetings will be held once a month during working hours, and nothing discussed will be passed on to supervisors or HR without the employee's permission.\nEmployees who serve as mentors will first attend a half-day training session on how to listen to concerns and how to avoid giving too much advice. Mentors will receive a monthly allowance, and mentoring will be treated as an important part of their duties. For details, please contact the Human Resources Department.",
