    "translation": "To all employees\nRe: Introduction of free-address seating (General Affairs Department)\nA working style combining work from home and office attendance has taken hold, and the average utilization of office desks now stays at around sixty percent. Desks that no one is sitting at still incur air-conditioning and lighting costs, so a review is needed from a cost standpoint as well. Therefore, in order to reduce unused desks and convert the freed-up space into areas for meetings and breaks, we will introduce free-address seating on the third and fourth floors of the head office starting next month. Fixed desks will be abolished, and employees who come to the office will choose any seat freely according to that day's work.\nPlease keep documents and personal belongings in the personal locker assigned one per person. When you leave for the day, please leave nothing on the desk. On days when a team wants to work together, a dedicated area can be secured through the reservation system. To address the worry that \"we won't know where our colleagues are,\" the seats of employees in the office will be viewable on the internal app.\nThe first three months after introduction will be a trial period, and we will adjust how the system is run while listening to your opinions.",
