    "translation": "To all employees\nRe: Recruiting participants for the data analysis training course (Human Resources Department)\nWhile the amount of data we handle in our work grows year by year, at present the only way to obtain people who can analyze it is to hire from outside. The company will therefore hold a training course in the basics of data analysis, with the aim of developing this talent in-house, and is recruiting twenty participants.\nThe course will run from October to December on Friday afternoons, ten sessions in all, taught by an instructor invited from outside. Attendance is treated as work, and the cost is borne by the company.\nEligible applicants are employees with at least two years of service who have obtained the approval of their department manager. No specialist knowledge such as statistics is required. Because exercises will use data from actual work, it is desirable — but not a condition — that you are currently involved in work that handles data.\nIf applications exceed the twenty places, selection will be by an essay of about 400 characters on the theme \"How will you apply what you learn in the course to your own work?\" The application deadline is September 15. The same course is planned for next fiscal year onward, so those not selected this time are encouraged to apply again.",
