    "translation": "To all employees\nRe: Updating the attendance management system (General Affairs Department)\nFrom October 1, we will switch to a new system for recording clock-in and clock-out times. Currently you record them by touching your IC card to the machine at the entrance, but under the new system, the times you log in to and out of your computer will be recorded automatically. The chore of reporting to General Affairs when you forget to touch your card will disappear.\nOn days you work from home, times are recorded through the same mechanism from your home computer, so there is no longer any need to report your working hours by email as before. How to handle work styles that do not use a computer, such as business trips, will be explained at the briefing sessions.\nIf a record is wrong, please apply for a correction from the system screen, stating the reason. Approval is given by the manager of your department.\nAlong with the changeover, three online briefing sessions for all employees will be held during September. The content is the same each time, so please attend just once, whichever session suits you. The schedule will be announced separately. Note that through September 30, recording with your IC card is still required as before.",
