    "translation": "I tried the foreign-language learning app \"Forest of Words\" for three months. Each study session is about five minutes. Points accumulate as in a game and your streak of consecutive study days is displayed, so as a mechanism for keeping you going, it is truly well made. In fact, I — a person who never sticks with anything for more than three days — did not miss a single day for ninety days, so I will praise this point honestly. Even on nights when I was too tired from work to sit at a desk, I could keep going under the covers with 'just five minutes.'\nThe problem is the content. It centers on practicing words and short sentences, and even after ninety days I did not become able to speak my own thoughts. There were moments when I felt the app's design was aimed less at learning outcomes than at \"extending the continuation record.\" There I was, choosing only easy review exercises for the sake of points. My record kept growing, yet I had little sense that my ability was.\nThat said, it is a fact that it built a habit of contact with a foreign language, even just five minutes a day, and its value as an entrance to learning is high. Don't expect to become able to speak with this app alone; combine it with other study, such as conversation practice. Used with that positioning, I can fully recommend it.",
